---
import ArticleLayout from '../../layouts/ArticleLayout.astro';
import NewsletterEmbed from '../../components/NewsletterEmbed.astro';

const contactHref = `mailto:hi@maxguerois.com?subject=${encodeURIComponent('Your article on life after leaving a startup')}&body=${encodeURIComponent("Hi Max,\r\n\r\nI loved your article about life after leaving a startup.\r\n\r\nHere's my experience:\r\n\r\n")}`;
---
<ArticleLayout
    title="Life after leaving my startup: Max Guerois"
    description="What leaving Lucis felt like, the struggles shared by 50+ founders, and what helped me move forward."
    ogUrl="https://maxguerois.com/newsletter/post-exit"
    ogImage="https://maxguerois.com/health-journey/post-exit.webp"
    ogImageAlt="Max lying in the grass beside an outdoor sauna"
    ogImageWidth={1600}
    ogImageHeight={1200}
>
    <div class="container">
        <a href="/newsletter" class="back">← All articles</a>

        <div class="article-meta">October 30, 2026</div>
        <h1 class="article-title">Life after leaving my startup</h1>

        <img
            class="article-img"
            src="/health-journey/post-exit.webp"
            alt="Max lying in the grass beside an outdoor sauna"
            width="1600"
            height="1200"
            fetchpriority="high"
            decoding="async"
        >

        <div class="article-body">
            <p>No one talks about what comes after you leave your company. <strong>So here’s my story.</strong></p>

            <p>I’ve spoken with <strong>more than 50 founders who sold their companies or left them</strong>, sometimes by choice, sometimes because they were pushed out.</p>

            <p>The same struggles came up every time.</p>

            <ul class="post-exit-points">
                <li>Losing your identity and motivation.</li>
                <li>Feeling like you’re worth nothing without the company.</li>
                <li>The pressure to start something new.</li>
                <li>The tension between decisions driven by ego and decisions driven by instinct (this is really, really hard).</li>
            </ul>

            <p>A lot of founders go through this.</p>

            <p>They don’t talk about it publicly because they’re afraid of complaining about “rich people’s problems” or sounding out of touch.</p>

            <p>For me, <strong>the strangest period of my life came after I left Lucis, my first startup.</strong></p>

            <p><strong>I’ll be honest: it wasn’t easy.</strong></p>

            <p>And almost nothing can fix these problems.</p>

            <ul class="post-exit-points">
                <li>You can travel. It’s nice for a while, then you start feeling useless and guilty.</li>
                <li>You can go to the sauna as often as you want (I still do 1 session a week hehe), try every kind of therapy and all the wellness stuff you want.</li>
            </ul>

            <p>None of it changes the way you think.</p>

            <p>Or maybe you start looking inward, and yes, that helps.</p>

            <p><strong>But you can spend so much time</strong> analysing yourself that you end up doing nothing.</p>

            <p>A lot of founders stay silent because they feel ashamed to talk about it.</p>

            <p><strong>I’ll never forget that period. Here are a few things that helped me:</strong></p>

            <ul class="post-exit-points">
                <li>Talking to other founders who’ve been through the same thing.</li>
                <li>Spending time with people outside the startup world</li>
                <li>Making time for loved ones and meeting new people 👸❤️</li>
                <li>Talking or writing to make sense of what I was going through.</li>
            </ul>

            <p><strong>I’m curious how other founders felt after an acquisition, a sale or leaving their company.</strong></p>

            <p>Tell me your story at <a class="post-exit-contact" href={contactHref}>hi@maxguerois.com</a>.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="article-footer">
            <span class="author-line">By <a href="/">Max Guerois</a></span>
        </div>

        <div class="post-exit-subscribe">
            <NewsletterEmbed />
        </div>
    </div>
</ArticleLayout>

<style>
    .article-img { height: auto; }
    .post-exit-points {
        padding-left: var(--sp-6);
        margin: 0 0 var(--sp-6);
        color: var(--text-secondary);
        line-height: 1.75;
    }
    .post-exit-points li + li { margin-top: var(--sp-2); }
    .post-exit-contact {
        color: var(--text);
        text-decoration: underline;
        text-underline-offset: 3px;
    }
    .post-exit-contact:hover { color: var(--accent); }
    .post-exit-subscribe { margin-top: var(--sp-12); }
</style>
